STORY-1889 PR 2 (hold/defer): one design point before I split merge_hold.rs (Phase B).
merge_hold.rs mixes four things:
(a) decisions: principal_is_recused, human_clear_actor, refusal_release/RefusalRelease, compose_holds, label_only_holds, and the corpus merge gate (corpus_merge_gate*, enforce_corpus_gate_before_merge);
(b) the hold READ path, i.e. whether a hold exists at all: read_hold, read_hold_record, parse_hold_marker, hold paths, and unrecorded_marker_removals (fail-closed tamper detection);
(c) the record types (MergeHoldRecord, PrincipalIdentity, HoldReasonKind, ...);
(d) plumbing: marker writes, forge label sync and definitions, pinned-change fetch, stray-marker adoption.
PROPOSAL: (a)+(b)+(c) move to gate/merge_hold_core.rs and (d) stays in merge_hold.rs, which then leaves the floor. Rationale: a change to (b) or (c) can make a hold invisible, for example read_hold returning None or a serde default dropping recused_principals. That is a loosening, so it belongs on the floor. (d) can only fail to PLACE or LABEL a hold, which stays reviewer-gated and is visible.
Also in PR 2: the merge-hold clear TTY-floor refusal in merge_hold_cmd.rs is extracted into the gate with its string unchanged. The merge_hold.rs inline tests split by subject: tests of (a)-(c) go to gate/tests/, the rest to src/tests/.
Reply if you want (b) or (c) left outside instead. Otherwise I proceed with this split.
